#1262 NEEDS A DATABASE — DOCKER FOR #1262 ONLY, UNDER THESE RULES. Docker is permitted for #1262 ONLY; every other PR runs with NO Docker action of any kind. The gate's own disposable Postgres binds on 127.0.0.1:55419 ONLY — 55410-55418 belong to the LIVE Seat B 29th: never bind, connect to or probe them beyond the `lsof` census. Before binding, PROVE THE PORT FREE against a control: `lsof -nP -iTCP:55419 -sTCP:LISTEN` == 0 AND a control that fires on this box (`lsof -nP -iTCP -sTCP:LISTEN` has > 0 lines; `:5432` is the native Postgres) — a zero from an instrument that cannot see a listener proves nothing. Use the image docker-compose.yml names (READ it; never `latest`; `postgres:15-alpine` is present locally), throwaway credentials generated 0600 inside YOUR report dir and never printed, the init dir bind-mounted read-only, and an ANONYMOUS volume only (no named volume, no host data dir); migrate with the GRADED tree's `scripts/run-migrations.sh` + `migrations/` copied into the container (say which tree; gate24T2c's #1258 changes that script — if it has merged, say so). Every DB variable the file reads points at YOUR :55419 database — TEST_DATABASE_URL, DATABASE_URL, TEST_PLATFORM_DATABASE_URL, PLATFORM_DATABASE_URL — and your shell exports no other DATABASE_URL (print the variable NAMES and the host:port of each, never a password). `:5432` LISTENS on the box (the native Postgres) — NEVER connect to it. Record the container id and its anonymous volume id at start. TORN DOWN AND PROVEN GONE at the end, even on failure (a trap in your own script): `docker rm -f -v <your container>`; then the container absent from `docker ps -a` (0 matches), YOUR anonymous volume id absent from `docker volume ls` (0 matches), `:55419` listeners 0 against the control; the volumes that are NOT yours (0ec12181dd37… and 0187e1998e06… at drafting — re-list them at your start) untouched, byte-for-byte the same list minus nothing. A container or volume of yours left behind = a finding against the GATE, reported first in your mail.

